"""Derive SkyyZones/build_skyyzones_0.2.2.py from SkyyZones/build_skyyzones_0.2.1.py (READY candidate of round wg0710; generated by
tools/zones_0_2_1_patch.py - never re-run that one for this). Edit THIS patch, never the generated script. Every anchor is asserted; at
the end every change is undone on a copy and compared with 0.2.1 (tools/soundpass_gen.Patch). Line endings kept.
Run:  python tools/zones_0_2_2_patch.py   then   python SkyyZones/build_skyyzones_0.2.2.py   (never --deploy)
Harness: python SkyyZones/test_skyyzones_0.2.2.py [--keep]

0.2.2 = round zones022. Skyy 2026-10-23 (inside their Mining shard, copper ore nodes, Collection Copper Ore 258/500): "ore on the shard should
 be protected. so if i break it by hand, it turns to stone then regenerates. just like it will in the world when i make the server world."
 WHOLE-WORLD REGROW BY WORLD-NAME PREFIX (regen.properties, Server Setup -> Zones -> Regrowing blocks, live):
  regen.worldPrefix       = skyy-shard-  (comma list of name starts, any case; empty = off). Every world whose name starts with one is ONE
                            whole-world regrow area - only for the types below, only for BREAKS: a hand- (or mob-) broken block of one of
                            those types gives its normal vanilla drop (Mining XP + collection exactly once, as a zone regrow), turns into
                            the placeholder, then grows back on its regrow.<type> timer (copper 4 s ... onyxium 15 s, gem 30 s, x
                            regen.speedMult / jitter). Worlds starting skyy-island- (players' islands) are NEVER matched (refused in
                            Server Setup, skipped at run time). A spot inside a region keeps the region's rules (regions decide first).
  regen.prefixTypes       = copper,iron,gold,silver,thorium,cobalt,adamantite,mithril,onyxium,gem (the ores; logs / crops refused: they
                            wait for Z3 whole-tree / crop-stage regrow, and SkyyShards already re-paints broken crops / trunks on AIR
                            itself; stone is not breakable in a shard - SkyyShards' shard:fn:allowed lets only crops, Ore_* and trunks break).
  regen.prefixPlaceholder = Rock_Stone (Skyy: "it turns to stone"; refused when it is a block of one of the prefix types). Not Rock_Bedrock
                            here: a shard's ore nodes stand on a stone floor and nothing in a shard world can break stone, and the waiting
                            spot refuses every break / dig / place anyway ("Growing back - wait a moment.").
 Everything else in such a world behaves as before (placing, using, building, totems, pads, portal, other blocks: SkyyZones does nothing
 there - SkyyShards / SkyyIslands' own guards decide). Builder mode breaks start no regrow (as in regions). zones.on / regen.enabled off
 switch it off too. The engine pieces are the 0.2.0 ones unchanged (journal FIRST, then the engine breaks it; placeholder pass; timer;
 restart safety; /zones restore all; regen off = all back): the only engine-side change is ZRegen.broke taking the prefix placeholder.
 SkyyShards interplay (read from build_skyyshards_0.4.6.py, no SkyyShards change): totem production + Collect are lazy maths (no block reads,
 no block breaks), so regrowing never changes Collect counts; ShFill paints gatherables only where the block is AIR, so it never fights the
 placeholder (a re-paint between the break and our placeholder pass = the pass sees the ore back and drops its entry - no 2nd drop).
 FIX vs a naive hook: the pass's re-index check (an entry whose spot no longer has a regrow type is forced back) now asks ZRules.regrowType
 (region type, else the prefix type) - else every prefix-world entry would be forced back at its first pass.
 FIX 2 (found by this harness, a 0.2.0 bug that shards make common): ZRw.snapshot wrote a spot mined again within 30 min of growing back
 as its D line AND its old V line; the replay turned it into a grown-back check, so after a restart it came back at once. Now a waiting
 spot is written only as D (no dupe / loss either way - it only grew back early).
 Saved data: no format change (same journal / snapshot lines, one regen/<world>.* pair per shard world). Config: 3 new regen.properties lines
 (missing lines read the defaults - no migration, no rewrite of Skyy's file). No new command / system / event / class.
 ROLLBACK to 0.2.1: run /zones restore all first (or Server Setup -> Zones -> Restore all) - 0.2.1 would otherwise force every waiting
 shard-world entry back at its first pass (harmless: they grow back at once). FLOOR: needs SkyyZones 0.2.1 with or before it (derived
 from it; deploys with SkyyWorldGen 0.7.10).
"""
